From: Enrique Magallon <dev.ace.93.03@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:49:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Swipe 20 mm per workspace in the overview

60 mm per workspace was four times the finger travel of cosmic-comp's
own swipe outside the overview (150 accelerated units, about 15 mm).
Devices that emit synthetic swipes are tuned to the compositor's
distance, so in the overview a normal stroke moved less than half a
workspace and snapped back: a Magic Mouse through mousetouch only
switched with an abrupt flick. 20 mm keeps a real touchpad comfortable
and brings both distances in line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Hjqk95EtWyxLg63zr44Nju
---
 src/swipe.rs | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/swipe.rs b/src/swipe.rs
index 8f48e6a..35c9b32 100644
--- a/src/swipe.rs
+++ b/src/swipe.rs
@@ -22,9 +22,12 @@ use std::{collections::VecDeque, sync::OnceLock, time::Instant};
 use crate::backend::ExtWorkspaceHandleV1;
 use cosmic::cctk::wayland_client::protocol::wl_output;
 
-/// Finger travel, in mm, for one full workspace. Override with
-/// `COSMIC_WORKSPACES_SWIPE_MM` to tune without rebuilding.
-const DEFAULT_PAGE_MM: f64 = 60.0;
+/// Finger travel, in mm, for one full workspace. Close to cosmic-comp's
+/// own swipe outside the overview (150 accelerated units, ~15 mm), so a
+/// touchpad and synthetic swipes (e.g. mousetouch) feel the same in and out
+/// of the overview. Override with `COSMIC_WORKSPACES_SWIPE_MM` to tune
+/// without rebuilding.
+const DEFAULT_PAGE_MM: f64 = 20.0;
 /// Velocity samples older than this are ignored (cosmic-comp `HISTORY_LIMIT`).
 const HISTORY_MS: u32 = 100;
 /// How far a fling coasts after release: `velocity * PROJECTION_S` pages.
